WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.125
What happens when 800 of the world's most elite footballers...

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:06.083
and their managers live together under one roof?

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:07.708
Players stop being polite...

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:09.791
and start getting Re-al.

00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:10.583
This is...

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:11.666
The Champions.

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:13.833
I don't call them free kicks.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.958
I call them free goals.

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:18.916
It's true that I sleep with all my hat trick balls.

00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:21.916
I have so many now I'm worried I might contract an STD.

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:23.583
A Sweet Transfer Deal.

00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.666
Uh, hello!

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:27.625
This was filmed two weeks before the air date, so, uh...

00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:29.958
could you let me know in the comments if I've been sacked yet?

00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.333
I score hat tricks like it's my job.

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:34.125
Wait, that is your job, though.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:35.375
Right. So that is good.

00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:48.041
It’s high time the media gave us keepers our due!

00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:49.625
Yeah! They don't appreciate us!

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:51.708
OK, OK. Yes, we all agree.

00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:54.291
But...we are moving on to new business.

00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:55.666
Uh, I would like to mention that

00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:57.708
sometimes our own clubs don’t appreciate us.

00:00:57.708 --> 00:00:58.916
OK. Danke, Keylor.

00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:00.208
Now, does anyone have anything

00:01:00.208 --> 00:01:03.041
that's not about being underappreciated?

00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:05.083
I want to say something.

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:07.791
I think that keepers should at least have the option

00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:10.375
to wear the same kit as the rest of the squad.

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:10.916
Right?

00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:13.666
All right. Here's my proposal. OK, listen.

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:16.791
I know. I’m a Yank. But I gotta—just hear me out, hear me out.

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:19.666
So, goalies should be able to wear big hats

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:21.541
that can cover the entire goal.

00:01:21.541 --> 00:01:25.125
So, I mean, you could just basically sit on your butt,

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:28.458
and your hat would block the whole goal!

00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:30.875
All right. Anyone else?

00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:32.875
I’d like to introduce a new motion.

00:01:33.708 --> 00:01:36.708
The chair recognizes Germany's No. 2.

00:01:36.708 --> 00:01:38.291
I think it’s time we have a vote

00:01:38.291 --> 00:01:40.583
for a new president of the Goalkeepers Union.

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.708
Don’t get me wrong, Manu has changed the game for keepers,

00:01:45.708 --> 00:01:48.666
but he needs to admit that he is no longer the face

00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:49.625
of the keeper position.

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:51.375
I...uh...

00:01:51.375 --> 00:01:52.500
Is this the keepers’ union?

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.375
Hey! No strikers allowed!

00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:56.458
It's OK. I’m not a striker. I’m an attacking midfielder.

00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:58.583
Same thing. No outfield players!

00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.833
Get outta here, bare-hander!

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:03.375
It’s urgent! I need to speak to you or else we’re all going to die.

00:02:06.041 --> 00:02:07.625
Why is that so funny?

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:10.625
My dear Raumdeuter, do you think us keepers,

00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:15.000
for all our time in solitude, have not pondered our own mortality?

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.000
No. You don't understand. This is an emergency!

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.458
If we do not act, Earth will be destroyed by Thursday.

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.541
Oh, no. I have a match on Thursday.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.666
So, why should we listen to you?

00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:27.916
For those of you who don’t know me,

00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:31.125
I was a very important and relevant player until, like, a year ago.

00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:34.125
My name is Thomas Muller, aka The Raumdeuter,

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:37.375
which roughly translates to space investigator or interpreter.

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:38.916
It's very cool actually, but...

00:02:38.916 --> 00:02:40.541
Get on with it, striker!

00:02:40.541 --> 00:02:41.750
OK. Right, right. Sorry.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.458
So I was investigating the space...like space-space,

00:02:44.458 --> 00:02:46.083
when I noticed something in the sky...

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:48.875
a giant meteor heading straight for Earth!

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.958
So what do you expect us to do?

00:02:51.958 --> 00:02:53.708
You are all the best in the world

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:57.166
when it comes to stopping things from hitting their target, right?

00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:59.250
I’m asking you, goalkeepers...

00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.416
to save the Earth!

00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:08.708
So we are supposed to just fly up into space and, uh, punch a meteor?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.333
I haven’t...figured that part out yet.

00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:16.083
I have an idea.

00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:17.416
Who the hell are you?

00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:21.541
Andriy Pyatov. Starting keeper. Shakhtar Donetsk.

00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:24.708
I think I know how we can stop this meteor.

00:03:40.416 --> 00:03:43.958
Gentlemen, meet…ze gigantsky mega vratar.

00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:46.541
Also known as Goaltron.

00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:47.708
Goaltron?

00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:49.958
After the meltdown at Chernobyl,

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:53.291
the Soviet apparatchiks proposed a secret plan

00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:58.041
to send giant goalie robot to ‘boot’ the reactor core into space.

00:03:58.041 --> 00:04:00.583
But the plan was ultimately deemed too stupid,

00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:03.166
and Goaltron was stored away indefinitely.

00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:04.750
How do you know all of this?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.458
I used to be backup goalie for Pripyat Roentgens.

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:10.083
So how does it work?

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.791
It is piloted by five goalkeepers.

00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:16.250
Four controlling each limb, and one in the head.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.416
That means we’ll need our top five goalies, so I’m out.

00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:22.958
Right. OK. Ederson, Alisson, you take the legs.

00:04:22.958 --> 00:04:25.125
Oblak, De Gea, the arms.

00:04:25.125 --> 00:04:27.166
And I'll take the head.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:30.375
Um...I mean...I don’t know if you’re top 5.

00:04:30.375 --> 00:04:34.250
What? I’m Manuel Neuer. The original sweeper-keeper.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.166
Manuel, nobody is denying your historical greatness.

00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:40.875
But you've had injuries. You're getting older.

00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:42.166
It happens to the best of us.

00:04:42.166 --> 00:04:44.375
But...who would you replace me with?

00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:46.833
Ter Stegen!?

00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:50.583
He can’t be the leader; he can’t even decide on a first name! 

00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:51.958
Oh, and you’ll lead us into space

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.416
like the time you led us up the field against South Korea?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.416
There’s no time for this. I will drive.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.666
Uh...let’s just go with the two Germans.

00:05:06.541 --> 00:05:10.458
OK, folks, this thing is coming in fast. We need to guess a direction.

00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:10.791
It’s coming left!

00:05:10.791 --> 00:05:13.166
No, you vollpfosten! It’s right. We need to dive right!

00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:16.083
I think we need to rush it and slide tackle it in open space.

00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:17.208
Agreed. Full thrust.

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:18.125
I don’t know, boys.

00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:20.250
I think we stay on our line and get a better read on it.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.291
Yeah. Good idea.

00:05:21.291 --> 00:05:22.625
Nein! We need to press!

00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:26.291
Nein! Manuel, nein! You’re so a-neuer-ing. Stay back! Stay back!

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:33.416
Oh...scheisse!

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:58.125
Ugh, I hate when I have to be subbed.

00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:00.166
Unless it's to this channel!

00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:02.791
Click "subscribe" button so you can sit and watch.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.041
Just like me!

